$b['An enormous purple dragon curls around the wearers arm while the head occupies the shoulder and a huge claw appears to grab the forearm from above'] = 'Two panels side by side on one image, divided down the middle. LEFT PANEL: the tattoo design alone on a plain white background, shown flat exactly as described, no body, drawn large so it fills most of the panel. RIGHT PANEL: Studio photograph of a real person''s body showing the same exact tattoo where described, healed tattoo on real skin in soft even light, the rest of the body modestly covered by simple plain clothing, only the tattooed area bare, plain seamless light grey studio backdrop - no room, no furniture, no scenery. The tattoo in both panels is identical. The tattoo: An enormous purple dragon curls around the wearers arm while the head occupies the shoulder and a huge claw appears to grab the forearm from above. Monumental, colorful, aggressive. In the right panel it is on a man, shoulder through forearm. Create exceptional contemporary New School tattoo artwork. REALITY IS OPTIONAL. PERSONALITY IS NOT. New School is a visual language built through intentional exaggeration, powerful silhouette, dimensional color, bold variable outlines, extreme perspective, expressive anatomy, graphic clarity and enormous personality. Do not confuse New School with generic cartoons. Do not make everything cute. Do not make everything funny. Do not create childrens illustration. Do not simply enlarge the eyes of an ordinary subject. EXAGGERATE THE THING THAT MAKES THE SUBJECT AWESOME. If the subject is a dragon, exaggerate the head, jaw, horns, claws, wings, movement or scale. If the subject is a skull, exaggerate the jaw, eye sockets, fracture, depth or perspective. If the subject is an animal, exaggerate the feature that expresses its personality. If the subject is a person, exaggerate expression, perspective, fashion, movement, hair, hands or attitude. If the subject is a machine, exaggerate the wheel, engine, lens