 Skeletons. Demons. Angels. Monsters. Dark fantasy. Horror. Mythology. Cars. Motorcycles. Machines. Fashion. Street culture. Architecture. Nature. Sea life. Birds. Insects. Objects. Food. Space. Surreal worlds. Impossible creatures. Abstract concepts. NEW SCHOOL IS THE STYLE. THE SUBJECT IS NOT THE STYLE. Do not repeat the same smiling animals, giant eyeballs, food characters or cartoon skulls simply because they are common New School imagery. Push artistic ambition. The body must influence the composition. THE BODY CAN BECOME PART OF THE PERSPECTIVE. Use shoulder curvature to increase volume. Use forearm length for approaching or receding forms. Use thighs for extreme depth and large characters. Use calves for vertical movement. Use knees and elbows as rotational centers when appropriate. Use ribs for wrapping forms. Use the chest for aggressive foreground scale. Use the back for rare world-building compositions. Do not simply place rectangular illustrations onto the body. Allow creatures and objects to wrap, project, turn, disappear and reappear with the anatomy. Most tattoos should remain realistic projects for actual tattoo clients. Use small and medium pieces throughout the collection. Use large pieces when the idea requires greater depth. Reserve full sleeves, backs and chest projects for exceptional concepts. Avoid visual clutter. New School can contain tremendous information, but the primary silhouette should still read from a distance. The viewer should understand the dominant subject before discovering secondary details. Avoid generic cartoon rendering. Avoid random rainbow palettes. Avoid identical oversized eyes. Avoid endless goofy facial expressions. Avoid childish clip art. Avoid making every animal smile. Avoid making every skull funny. Avoid flat compositions. Avoid equal line weight everywhere. Avoid using graffiti merely as meaningless background. Avoid using color without hierarchy. Avoid confusing New School with Neo-Traditional. NEO-TRADITIONAL generally preserves more believable proportion, decorative illustration and controlled dimensionality. NEW SCHOOL deliberately pushes proportion, perspective, expression, volume and anatomy beyond reality. NEW SCHOOL CAN BREAK REALITY WHILE REMAINING VISUALLY COHERENT. BIG SHAPES. BIG COLOR. BIG DEPTH. BIG PERSONALITY. DARK WHEN IT WANTS TO BE. BEAUTIFUL WHEN IT WANTS TO BE. WEIRD WHEN IT WANTS TO BE. THE STYLE STAYS NEW SCHOOL. THE IMAGINATION HAS NO SPEED LIMIT'
